Z||000000||Galen||11-23-2001||03:18 PM||||88 2.5 coupe..<P>should the rear calipers be able to be 'wiggled' any at all? & should the pads be able to be moved(i'm guessing yeah)<P>------------------<BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT></B> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||11-23-2001||06:33 PM||||Yeah,the whole caliper floats on the outside of the mounting bolts,or "sliders".<BR>Since the piston pushes only in one direction...||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||11-25-2001||04:02 AM||||They shouldn't move MUCH!!<P>A tiny bit is normal in a floating caliper (never liked the design) but excessive play could mean that you've got either worn slider pins, or worn caliper slides themselves  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Yeah, the pads should be movable a little.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
